[PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]
## Consolidated Experience from Similar Tasks
Consolidated lessons from prior failures: (1) Never assume a target object is present or locatable; a failed find/search means the object may be elsewhere or the search method was invalid. Inspect the environment and search plausible containers or alternate locations before proceeding. (2) Never assume an action succeeded just because it was attempted; always verify applicability and check environment feedback. Actions like open or pick-up can fail if preconditions are unmet. (3) Before interacting with an object, ensure the robot has navigated to its location and is close enough; proximity is a precondition for pick-up. Do not assume an object is held unless the pick-up action explicitly succeeds. (4) Adapt by using valid skills and known storage locations, and confirm each state change before moving to the next step.

## Preliminary Thinking
1. Locate the ladle: search likely areas such as countertops, sink, drawers, or cabinets. If it is not immediately found, check plausible containers or alternate locations. Do not assume it is present; verify search results. 2. If the ladle is inside a closed container, attempt to open it only after confirming the open action is valid for that object; if the open action fails, search elsewhere. 3. Navigate to the ladle and verify proximity before picking it up. Attempt pick-up only when close enough, then confirm the ladle is held. 4. Navigate to a sink or water source. If the ladle is already at the sink, proceed; otherwise bring it there or position it for rinsing. 5. Execute the rinse action on the ladle, ensuring the ladle and water source are valid targets and the robot is properly positioned. Verify the ladle is clean/wet after rinsing. 6. Navigate to the table while holding the ladle. Place/move the ladle onto the table and confirm successful placement. Throughout: check action feedback at every step; if an action is invalid or fails, reassess object location, proximity, or action applicability rather than assuming success.
[/PERSISTENT EXPERIENCE GUIDANCE]